    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_core_one_exceptional_only_distance_three_dihedral_subgroup_norm_descent",
    "title": "Rate-half distance-three dihedral subgroup-norm descent",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On either surviving rank-two dihedral branch, the sparse subgroup norm Res_X(X^N-1,Q) descends to an orbit resultant with a degree-at-most-(2e+1) value polynomial. The antipodal quotient locator is U^(N/2)-1; the constant-product quotient locator is the exact square-root part of D_N(U,c)-2 after removing zero or two fixed-point factors. Exact-degree split slopes are equivalently detected by splitting the descended polynomial over this quotient set.",
